card.statement:
Given $L=(l_{ij})\in\mathbb{C}^{\frac{n(n+1)}{2}}$, denote by $T(L)$ the array

\begin{center}

\Stone{ {$l_{n1}$}}\Stone{ {$l_{n2}$}} $\cdots$ \Stone{ {$l_{n,n-1}$}}\Stone{ {$l_{nn}$}}
[0.2pt]
\Stone{ {$l_{n-1,1}$}} $\cdots$ \Stone{ {$l_{n-1,n-1}$}}
[0.3cm]
$\cdots$ $\cdots$ $\cdots$
[0.3cm]
\Stone{ {$l_{21}$}}\Stone{ {$l_{22}$}}
[0.2pt]
\Stone{ {$l_{11}$}}

\end{center}
Such an array will be called a Gelfand-Tsetlin tableau of height $n$. A Gelfand-Tsetlin tableau of height $n$ is called standard if
$l_{ki}-l_{k-1,i}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$ and $l_{k-1,i}-l_{k,i+1}\in\mathbb{Z}_{> 0}$ for all $1\leq i\leq k\leq  n$.
